title RecruitBook Batch 1 — Authentication System Context

left to right direction

' ============================================================
' ACTORS (far left) — interact ONLY through Browser / Client
' ============================================================

actor "Public Visitor" as PublicVisitor
actor "Authenticated User" as AuthUser
actor "Student" as Student
actor "Counselor" as Counselor
actor "Admissions Officer" as AdmissionsOfficer
actor "Platform Administrator" as PlatformAdmin

Student --|> AuthUser
Counselor --|> AuthUser
AdmissionsOfficer --|> AuthUser
PlatformAdmin --|> AuthUser

' ============================================================
' CLIENT TIER (next) — single entry point for all actors
' ============================================================

component "User Browser / Client" as Browser <<external>>

' ============================================================
' RECRUITBOOK APPLICATION TIER (center)
' App → Route Guard → Protected Routes
' ============================================================

rectangle "RecruitBook Application Tier" as AppTier #F1F5F9 {

  component "RecruitBook Next.js App" as App

  component "Route Guard / Access Policy\n(server-side · middleware / layout)" as Guard #FEF3C7

  rectangle "Protected Dashboard Routes" as Routes #F8FAFC {
    card "/student/dashboard\n/counselor/pending\n/counselor/dashboard\n/admissions/pending\n/admissions/dashboard\n/admin/dashboard\n/unauthorized" as RouteList
  }
}

' ============================================================
' EXTERNAL SYSTEMS (right)
' ============================================================

component "Supabase Auth" as Auth <<external>>
database "RecruitBook Application Database\n(PostgreSQL)" as DB
component "Email Service" as Email <<external>>

' ============================================================
' ACTOR FLOWS — through Browser / Client only
' ============================================================

PublicVisitor --> Browser : register / login / reset
AuthUser --> Browser : access dashboards / logout
PlatformAdmin --> Browser : approve / suspend / reject

' ============================================================
' MAIN FLOWS — trust boundaries labeled on the arrows
' ============================================================

Browser --> App : TB-1 · registration, login, logout,\npassword reset requests
App --> Auth : TB-2 · credential + session requests\n(sign-up, sign-in, verify, reset, sign-out)
App --> DB : TB-3 · create / read profile,\nread + update role / account_status
Auth --> Email : TB-4 · verification +\npassword reset emails
App --> Guard : route request + Supabase session
Guard --> Routes : TB-5 · authorize → dashboard / pending,\ndeny → /unauthorized

' Route Guard consults the database for the authorization decision
Guard --> DB : read role / account_status

' ============================================================
' SECURITY NOTES (instead of extra arrows)
' ============================================================

note bottom of Auth
  Supabase Auth authenticates
  credentials and manages sessions.
  It does not decide application
  authorization.
end note

note bottom of DB
  Source of truth. Stores role,
  account_status, approval state,
  suspension state, and audit logs.
end note

note bottom of Guard
  A valid Supabase session is required
  but not sufficient. Protected routes
  also require database role/account_status
  checks. UI hiding alone is not
  authorization — checks are enforced
  server-side (middleware / layout).
  • Pending Counselor / Admissions →
    pending page, not full dashboard.
  • Suspended or invalid role/status →
    /unauthorized.
end note

note top of App
  Public registration allows Student,
  Counselor, and Admissions Officer only.
  Platform Administrator accounts cannot
  be created through public registration
  (seeded / manually provisioned).
end note

legend bottom
  Trust boundaries
  TB-1 Browser ↔ RecruitBook App
  TB-2 RecruitBook App ↔ Supabase Auth
  TB-3 RecruitBook App ↔ Application Database
  TB-4 Supabase Auth / App ↔ Email Service
  TB-5 RecruitBook App ↔ Protected Routes
endlegend

